    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented soft-duplicate detection for `POST /api/owners`: a new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created, with `possibleDuplicate: true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id \u2014 otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges, following the existing `namesakeCount`/`bulkSignupWarning` pattern (computed at creation, persisted, mapped to the response):\n\n- **New pipeline step** `FlagPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 runs before `SaveOwner` (so `findAll()` excludes the new row), compares against each existing owner on normalized `lastName` + equal `postcode` + differing canonical telephone, and records the lowest matching id.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `flagPossibleDuplicate` between `flagBulkSignup` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) columns with accessors.\n- **Schema** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to all four `schema.sql` files (the test profile is hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, and the test reads the fields back via a separate `GET`, so persistence is required).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the `Owner` response schema (MapStruct maps them by name; jackson omits the null `possibleDuplicateOf` when false).\n- **Tests** \u2014 the provided `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` (true branch) plus an added `uniqueOwnerIsNotPossibleDuplicate` (false branch).\n\n`./mvnw -o test`: **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\nOne pre-existing MapStruct warning about unmapped target properties on the request\u2192entity mapping (`toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`) now also lists the two new fields \u2014 this is the same benign warning already present for `customerCode`, `householdId`, etc. (server-computed fields legitimately not set from the request body), not an error.",
